review_comments.body:
it's interesting that we weren't checking the type here before, and I'm not sure we should? Currently unmount was doing:

```js
unmount(vnode, removeDom = true) {
  if (IS_COMPONENT(vnode)) {
    // unmount (but do not remove) all children:
    for (child of vnode.children) unmount(child, removeDom: false)
    if (removeDom) vnode.dom.remove()
  }
  else if (removeDom === false) {
    vnode.dom.remove()
  }
}
```

So in the current algo, when unmounting a component, we remove the DOM node for each subtree when encountering its outermost vnode (regardless of whether its a component or element vnode).

I suspect we could revise this to instead only ever remove the DOM node for element vnodes, but if we're doing that I think this whole function could be simplified (one typeof at the top).

